cff-version: 1.2.0
message: >-
  If you use this repository, please cite it together with the UN-CEBD
  Scanner Data handbook and the Zenodo source dataset.
title: COICOP Classification Notebook
type: software
authors:
  - family-names: Palumbo
    given-names: Luigi
repository-code: 'https://github.com/paluigi-moltis/coicop-classification-notebook'
abstract: >-
  Example Jupyter notebook for classifying scanner-data products into
  COICOP 2018 for CPI production, following the UN-CEBD Task Team on
  Scanner Data classification methodology (Methods 0-4, evaluation,
  class imbalance, production loop). Data: manual records from Zenodo
  10.5281/zenodo.18459651 (CC-BY-SA 4.0), augmented with deterministic
  synthetic attributes.
keywords:
  - COICOP
  - CPI
  - consumer price index
  - scanner data
  - classification
  - machine learning
  - official statistics
license: MIT
commit: main
